From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:30:00 -0400
Subject: windows: Stedding's keyboard map, the shortcut reference on every platform

Arc's keyboard on the views platforms (docs/features/windows.md N7): the
Mac's map (accelerators_cocoa.mm, global_keyboard_shortcuts_mac.mm) with
Cmd read as Ctrl and Option-Cmd as Ctrl+Alt, which is how Arc for Windows
spells it. In the shared !IS_MAC block of accelerator_table.cc: Ctrl+D
pins the tab in its Space and Ctrl+Shift+D shows or hides the address row
(Bookmark This Tab and Bookmark All Tabs keep their menu rows and lose
the keys), Ctrl+S collapses the sidebar (Save Page moves to Ctrl+Shift+S),
Ctrl+Shift+K clears the Space, Ctrl+Shift+C copies the clean link (Inspect
keeps F12 and Ctrl+Shift+I), Ctrl+Shift+2 and Ctrl+Shift+1 are the page
and full-page screenshots, Ctrl+Shift+P opens the command bar in actions
mode -- the system print dialog moves to Ctrl+Alt+P, and the print
preview's link says so. Windows alone: Alt+1-9 for the Spaces, and a
Ctrl+Alt map -- Ctrl+Alt+Left/Right between Spaces and with Shift the tab
across, Ctrl+Alt+Up/Down the rows and with Shift their move,
Ctrl+Alt+Shift+2 the region screenshot, Ctrl+Alt+Shift+C the Markdown
link, Ctrl+Alt+Shift+N a Blank Window -- added past Chromium's Ctrl+Alt
check the way its own debug map is (docs/HANDOFF.md, trap 42). The
tab-group chords are Linux's alone now, as on the Mac (menus M6).

The row numbers show while Ctrl is held (tabs R11); the Space chips keep
their glyphs on Windows, Alt+N being too long for a 24 DIP chip. The
tab menu names the chord beside Pin to This Space, Copy Link and Copy
Link as Markdown on every platform (menus M1): the verbs map to the
browser commands their keys are bound to, which nothing did before.

The shortcut reference (docs/features/shortcuts.md Z6) reads the
platform's own table through GetAcceleratorForCommandId, its divergence
rows and notes are the platform's, and its handler and unit test build
everywhere, so chrome://settings/stedding carries the block on Windows
(windows N5). The settings sub-labels and the welcome flow name Ctrl and
Alt where they named the Mac's glyphs.

Why: docs/features/windows.md N7. Every Stedding key is documented as
Arc's, and the Windows preview had none of them.
Removable when: Chromium's accelerator tables come from one
cross-platform source, or Stedding's keys move to a table of their own.
